            <ArticleTitle>[Update of the relationship between erectile dysfunction and endothelial function].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>632-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endothelial function plays a very important role in the process of erection. Erectile dysfunction (ED) and coronary artery disease (CAD) overlap in risk factors, aetiology and clinical outcomes. Endothelial dysfunction is considered to be their shared aetiological factor. There is growing evidence that patients presenting with ED should be investigated for CAD, even if with no symptoms of the problem. Earlier diagnosis of ED can facilitate prompt intervention, reduce long-term complications, especially the risk of CAD, and provide effective treatment for ED.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
